Vestira Koi is a dwarven woman of [[Org/Sedecium|Sedecium]], the crew of a ship from beyond the [[Phenomena/Firmament|firmament]]. She has a long beard and black hair, and wears the service's sixteen-pointed star. She serves as the crew's liaison officer, trained to suppress the anomalies that space and time throw up and to make contact with the cultures Sedecium meets.

She walked the Party through the ritual of suppression over the ship's speaker grates, one glyph at a time, and warned them that the rite works by giving the thing being suppressed life, so that it can be fought and killed. She asks who she is dealing with before she says much. She knows the [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/index|Ashen Pact]] gods by their Thessian names.

Her work is contact, not engineering, and she says so when the Party asks after the ship's fuel: the icy blue liquid that runs its pipes is [[Phenomena/Godblood|Godblood]], synthetic, and dangerous to touch; Sedecium takes it on at fuel depots and does not make it in Siju, and it began trying to harvest [[Phenomena/Phlogiston|phlogista]] only after the wreck. She says Sedecium's original directive was to contain [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Esoterica|Gremory]], and to find what its logs call the entity, and that the crew cannot kill a Thessian without a spike of [[Phenomena/Holy Gold|holy gold]]. After the rescue she took charge of the survivors, asked the Party to help find the rest of her crew, and offered directions to Gremory.
